  "details": "Rather than Echo the numerous Canny posts about EAC, I'll move on to why a Mod browser would be a better idea.\nA mod browser would...\n- Keep the base game client light weight and simple, for those players with lower end PCs especially, where Framerate is already a struggle.\n- Allow for Easy and Secure access to mods that could both be checked by Staff for TOS Breaches, and perhaps even user rated.\n- Boost creativity in the Community, enabling a new level of creativity in VRChat that only a few have attempted.\n- Be overall less work for VRChat, no longer having to pile extra code into the game for requested features, Now Players could create them and choose to use them or not!\n- Be good PR\n- Be another reason to get VRC+ if necessary, as many of the popular mods support having VRC+, Some even require it. (Although some should be free, such as Disability-Aid mods)\n- Enable account flagging of Accounts with Mods installed for purposes of bug reports, as mentioned in the website post.\nAnd the Negatives?\n- Probably takes a little more work to create than Easy anti-cheat\nI think a Mod browser would be a much more efficient, useful and Community friendly Update for VRChat, and could in fact inspire some players to get VRC+ Subsciptions, There is very little logical reason to get EAC over a mod browser, as EAC Will only anger Bad actors and with VRChat being a free game, they will find a way around eventually, This update is a bandaid.\nThank you.  - Nym",
